WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.542
Teacher midterm practice, question 34.

2
00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:08.221
True or false: during a tensile test, engineering stress will

3
00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:11.809
always have an equal or higher value than true stress.

4
00:00:13.509 --> 00:00:17.001
Engineering stress divides the force by the original area.

5
00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:19.687
True stress divides it by the current area.

6
00:00:20.307 --> 00:00:23.269
In tension the specimen gets thinner, so the current area

7
00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:26.231
is smaller, and the true stress is the higher one.

8
00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:31.033
The statement is backwards, so the answer is B: false.

9
00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:33.826
Do not reverse the inequality.

10
00:00:33.826 --> 00:00:36.653
In tension, true stress is the larger one.
